BACKGROUND: I have a way to get to 3.0j source, which I have hacked
significantly in the past for DEC UNIX System V and PC/DOS/286 platforms.
For reasons not worth getting into, I won't be getting the source back on
line unless I hit a worth-the-effort threshold.  This post is intended for
folks who have also hacked the source.  If I can get resolutions to most
of these nuisances, it can help me hit that threshold.

- For both PC and UNIX, I have hit occasions when, after restoring a
particularly good game, NetHack says  something like "finishing off %s",
where %s is expanded to a recent aquisition.  This usually bites me when I
am having my greatest games, like after I have used up my wand of wishing,
I'm still in the castle without intrinsic teleport control, and my most
recent aquisition is a blessed ring of teleport control.  Question: has
anybody identified where this bit of code is, and why it's there?

- I have also noticed on UNIX (don't know if this is true on a PC) that if
I recompile NetHack, old saved games no longer work.  The inventory is
scrogged (the text descriptions look like a random pasting of strings).
Question: Why is this?  (my first guess is something arcane about pointers
and structure alignment)

- Has anybody out there actually bothered to fix the bag-of-holding bug,
the pet-drops-gold bug, or the marillith-slices-a-worm bug?

- Has anybody actually implemented a mod that saves the charcter when
transitioning levels?  This one may be mostly for David Blume, who has
posted a comment that this might be fairly straightforward and worth
doing.

If anybody has ready-made patches available for this stuff, I'd be
interested in an emailed copy of your patch source.

